In the price ID section, you might want to mention that
for non-combat-wombat classes you can actually sell
weapons and armor to shopkeepers and you will be told
what they are for the mundane types.  Then you can use
any of the standard tricks to rob the shop to get your
items back.

I've used this to ID all sorts of orcish, dwarvish,
elvish and regular armor and weapons.  That is visored
helmet to helmet, crude dagger to orcish dagger and
such.  Price needs to be calculated for +/- number
and b/u/c status isn't included.

I don't know if it works on the interesting types, I
don't think so.

Also, one you've run a shopkeeper out of money it
stops working so feel free to buy stuff at full price
to keep him/her from running out if you do this a
lot.



